fix(effect-cluster): name a runner's Postgres pool after the runner

Against alchemy `packages/effect-cluster/src` at 33c10dd (2.0.0-beta.87). Apply from the
repository root with `git apply`; the text above the first `---` line is ignored.

## Problem

Effect Cluster 4.1.4 holds every shard of a runner as a session-level advisory lock on one
connection it reserves from the runner's SQL pool (`SqlRunnerStorage.ts`, `acquireLockConn`).
Another connection can read in `pg_locks` which backend holds a shard's lock, but not whose backend
it is: the bootstrap builds the runner's pool with `PgClient.layer({ url })`, so every session of
every runner carries `@effect/sql-pg` as its `application_name`, and behind a proxy or a load
balancer every session has the same `client_addr` too. On a Docker swarm overlay every session
arrives from the network's load-balancer address.

So nothing that commits on its own connection can establish that its runner owns a shard, which is
what the domain's commit fence (07) must establish before it lets a commit through.

## Fix

- `Host.ts` exports `runnerPoolName(host, port)`: `effect-cluster:<host>:<port>`. PostgreSQL keeps 63
  bytes of `application_name` and replaces characters outside printable ASCII; a name that would be
  cut or changed becomes `effect-cluster:#` plus an FNV-1a hash of `host:port` (16 + 8 bytes), so two
  runners never share a cut name and both sides compute the same one.
- The runner bootstrap (`internal/Bootstrap.ts`, `bootstrap`, the pool whose runners hold shards)
  builds that pool with `applicationName: runnerPoolName(host, RUNNER_PORT)`, from the same `host`
  and port it gives Effect as `ShardingConfig.runnerAddress`. The lock session Effect reserves from
  the pool carries the name, as do the pool's other sessions, which hold no locks.
- `runExternal` is left as it is: its pool serves a client-only gateway (`clientOnly: true`) that
  holds no shards; the external program it starts builds its own pool from `DATABASE_URL`.

No change to Effect: `PgClient.layer` already accepts `applicationName` (`@effect/sql-pg` 4.1.4,
`PgClient.ts`).

## Why it is safe

- `application_name` is informational to PostgreSQL; nothing in Effect or Alchemy reads it except
  07's fence.
- One setting on a pool the bootstrap already builds; operators gain runner names in
  `pg_stat_activity`.

## Failing case, and how it was reproduced

On a cluster (two runners and a front on Effect Cluster with PostgreSQL 17, on a single-node Docker
swarm on one workstation), the lock holders of the cluster's namespace:

```sql
SELECT a.application_name, a.client_addr, count(*)
FROM pg_locks l JOIN pg_stat_activity a ON a.pid = l.pid
WHERE l.locktype = 'advisory' AND l.classid = <namespace> AND l.objsubid = 2 AND l.granted
GROUP BY 1, 2;
```

Without this patch it returns two rows that differ only by pid, both `@effect/sql-pg` from the
load-balancer address: no connection can tell which runner holds a shard. With it, it returns
`effect-cluster:10.0.1.6:34431` and `effect-cluster:10.0.1.7:34431`, 150 shards each. After the lock
session is ended (`pg_terminate_backend`, or the 35 s `idle_session_timeout` of a paused runner),
the session Effect rebuilds carries the same name and takes the shards back. With 07, the paused
runner case held its invariant in each of six runs (07's description).

## Where it ran

- On a cluster: the deploys above, with and without this patch (the latter on an earlier version
  of the application), and 07's cases.
- In process: `runnerPoolName` itself (the cut-name form for a 70-character host).

## Depends on

Nothing; it touches only `packages/effect-cluster`. 07 imports `runnerPoolName` from it.

## The alternative, not taken

Effect could name the lock session itself: `SqlRunnerStorage`'s `acquireLockConn` would
`set_config('application_name', 'effect-cluster:<runner address>', false)` in the statement that
already sets the session's `idle_session_timeout`, or `RunnerStorage` would expose the lock
session's pid. Either works from inside Effect for every host. This patch needs no change to Effect,
because the pool the lock session is reserved from is the bootstrap's to build.
